  "reason": "Accept non-Latin-1 names and single bare declaration values. The combined patches change 19 patch-corpus trees and 47 seeded edits against committed C. Cases non-latin1-value-001, 002 and 009 repair lone identifier values. Case 005 differs because 0001 recognizes the dashed custom-property reference. The dimension and function cases (003 and 004), the excluded identifier continuations (006 through 008), and the scanner boundary controls (non-latin1-names-009 through 011) retain errors with changed recovery. The edit signatures cover the name and value fixes and their boundaries. No previously error-free tree changes in this comparison.",
  "retireWhen": "An approved CSS pin contains a fix for the name defect in upstream PR #105 or for the declaration-value defect reported in its comment. On that pin move, retire each covered patch and update the affected corpus expectations and known-gap records.",
